BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Water entry</h1>
On the open Atlantic in the default sea (7 m/s wind, a metre of swell): a
delta-glider ditches (70 m/s, sinking 2.4 m/s, nose up 8 deg, gear up) and
a ShuttlePB drops flat into the water at 9 m/s. The water must stop them
within plausible distances and loads, and leave them afloat, upright.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 51982.6685767396
  Script Tests/WaterEntryTest
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship DITCH
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET DITCH
  MODE Extern
  POS 4 0 -20
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 50.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_SHIPS
DITCH:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Landed Earth
  POS -70.0000 28.0000
  HEADING 90.00
  GEAR 0 0.0000
  PRPLEVEL 0:0.200 1:1.000
END
DROP:ShuttlePB
  STATUS Landed Earth
  POS -70.0000 28.0100
  HEADING 0.00
  PRPLEVEL 0:0.200
END
END_SHIPS
